<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34427" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pellēnē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πελλήνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Achaia</i>, <i>on the Gulf
				of Corinth</i>, <i>between Sicyon and
				Ægira</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 33, 15</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pellēnaeus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Pellenian;
			subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pellēnaei</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Pellene</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				4, 5, 6, § 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pellēnensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>Pellenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					33, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Timocrates,</span>”
				<i>of Pellene</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
